{
  "_about": "Category twin of the quotation pack guard (mig 0410 · PR-G). ONE list for both sides: lineTakesPacks(line, null) of linePacks.js (JS — the rule of every server gate) and the category expression that 0410 copies nine times (the trigger T2 with NEW., the gates and the two header SELECTs with l.). takesPacks = what BOTH sides answer for that line (proven on PGlite 0.5.8 = PostgreSQL 18.3 with the expression cut out of the migration, 15/10/2026). linePacks.test.mjs runs the JS side on every row; quotationPackGuardMigration.test.mjs checks that the migration carries categoryExpression verbatim. Changing lineCategoryCode / categoryOf so that a row flips = the database guard no longer matches the server gates: write a new migration for the trigger (0410 is frozen once run).",
  "categoryExpression": "COALESCE(CASE WHEN COALESCE(NEW.\"productId\", '') <> '' OR COALESCE(NEW.\"fgCode\", '') <> '' THEN substring(NEW.\"fgCode\" from '[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{3}') = '02-001' ELSE jsonb_typeof(NEW.metadata -> 'categoryCode') = 'string' AND NEW.metadata ->> 'categoryCode' = '02-001' END, false)",
